      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>chron</b> (Greek) and <b>temp</b>, <b>tempor</b> (Latin) = <b>time</b>. <b>ann</b>, <b>enn</b> = <b>year</b>. <b>nov</b> = <b>new</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "The list has five <i>chron</i> words: <b>chronic</b> (lasting a long time), <b>chronicle</b> (a record of events in time order), <b>chronological</b> (arranged by time), <b>synchronize</b> (make happen at the same time) and <b>anachronism</b> (something out of its time)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "chron",
            "temp"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "chron and temp (time)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "ann",
            "nov"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "ann (year) and nov (new)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>chronic</b><br>lasting a long time or coming back again and again",
            "<b>chron</b> <i>time</i> + -ic<br>→ “lasting through time”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>chronicle</b><br>a record of events in the order they happened",
            "<b>chron</b> <i>time</i> + -icle<br>→ “a record of the times”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>chronological</b><br>arranged in order of time",
            "<b>chron</b> <i>time</i> + log <i>reason, order</i> + -ical<br>→ “in time order”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>anachronism</b><br>something placed in the wrong time period",
            "ana- <i>back, against</i> + <b>chron</b> <i>time</i> + -ism<br>→ “a thing against its time”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>contemporary</b><br>living or happening at the same time; also, modern",
            "con- <i>with</i> + <b>tempor</b> <i>time</i> + -ary<br>→ “of the same time”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>extemporaneous</b><br>spoken or done without preparation",
            "ex- <i>out of</i> + <b>tempor</b> <i>time</i> + -aneous<br>→ “out of the moment (on the spot)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>perennial</b><br>lasting or returning year after year",
            "per- <i>through</i> + <b>enn</b> <i>year</i> + -ial<br>→ “through the years”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>annals</b><br>a year-by-year record of events; history",
            "<b>ann</b> <i>year</i> + -als<br>→ “yearly records”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>innovative</b><br>introducing new ideas",
            "in- <i>into</i> + <b>nov</b> <i>new</i> + -ative<br>→ “bringing in the new”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>novice</b><br>a beginner",
            "<b>nov</b> <i>new</i> + -ice<br>→ “someone new”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Spot the anachronism",
        "q": "In a play set in a medieval castle, a knight checks the time on his wristwatch. Why is that an <b>anachronism</b>?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>ana-</b> (back, against) + <b>chron</b> (time) + <b>-ism</b> (a thing).",
          "Literally: “a thing set against its time.”",
          "Wristwatches did not exist in medieval times, so the watch is in the wrong time period."
        ],
        "a": "It puts an object in a time period where it does not belong."
      },
